{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide","id":1218958,"title":"ed 3rd - Brawl Charm Guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-15T10:33:08-07:00","id":1218958,"title":"ed 3rd - Brawl Charm Guide","content":"Following the inspiration from the Melee Charm Guide that was posted here, a friend of mine, Omicronone, decided to do a Brawl Charm Guide, which is here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qm6VCooKWnZNhvjPgLEtSZ2p2Uso2pu4ViBAREXrAuQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Hope it's useful!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","user":"pcontop","date":". 05-18-2018, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T19:16:14-07:00","id":1219153,"title":"","content":"Neat! Brawl is my favorite Solar Ability, and I'd say your friend's guide is pretty spot on overall. The idea of separating how good a Charm is for each of the two broad Brawl archetypes was a good one as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T20:19:59-07:00","id":1219164,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised at your dismissal of Rapturous Cradle, given the uses you suggest for Burning Brand of Authority.<br /> <br /> If you drop one guy you've grappled in order to deal with a second guy, the first guy could be running away while you deal with the second. Burning Brand only works at close range, so Rapturous Cradle lets you grab the runaway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T14:18:17-07:00","id":1219427,"title":"","content":"One thing Rapturous Cradle does is let you drop someone down a cliff, let them suffer a long range fall, then pull them back into your grapple which may be better than a Savage attack. I agree Orange is probably the right color for it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T14:36:51-07:00","id":1219442,"title":"","content":"Also its cool someone else out there realized how good Inevitable Victory Meditation is - big thumbs up from me.<br /> <br /> Heaven Fury Smite is a great charm no doubt, but I've found in actual play I frequently want to follow up a big withering hit with a Simple-type charm, which HFS does not let you do. A small mark against it.<br /> <br /> The only charm whose position I strongly disagree with is Burning Fist Burial - that thing is way more niche than it might seem, and usually is a complete waste of motes. Brawl is so good at generating initiative (and damage in general) that adding raw decisive dice, even for 1m for 1d, is a pretty questionable exchange rate. Paying a 4m surcharge on top of that for the benefit of post-roll activation and a soft-cap on the number of damage dice you can add is not worth it. This may seem mindblowing considering how good post-roll activation generally is, but it's true. <br /> <br /> It's really bad if you only want to add a couple damage dice (6m for +2 dice?? In brawl??) and doesn't scale that well in efficiency for normal case uses. 10m for +6 dice is not good. Burning Fist Burial sucks and should be moved from blue to orange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T15:32:35-07:00","id":1219457,"title":"","content":"I will disagree with Shockwave Technique being hard to reset. Charms enhancing an attack can reset off of that very attack. So if you use Shockwave in combo with a decisive Crashing Wave Throw You will be able to reset the shockwave right away most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T20:44:26-07:00","id":1219524,"title":"","content":"This is pretty good, and I agree on most points! I suggest you throw a link to Madletter's Charm Cascade for reference in the OP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.madletter.net/rpg/exalted/cascades/v3/cascade_v3_brawl.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.madletter.net/rpg/exalted/cascades/v3/cascade_v3_brawl.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.madletter.net/rpg/exalted/cascades/v3/cascade_v3_brawl.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.madletter.net/rpg/exalted/cascades/v3/cascade_v3_brawl.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T22:23:30-07:00","id":1219537,"title":"","content":"Why such a negative rating of sledgehammer fist punch? Sure its a niche effect but reflexive feats of destruction can be handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T03:06:50-07:00","id":1219568,"title":"","content":"I will say in defense of Sledgehammer Fist Punch, we actually came across a scenario last night where it would have been useful. Our brawler wanted to smash through a wall, but at her strength could only bash through it &quot;slowly&quot; and she was pressed for time. Sledgehammer Fist Punch would have allowed her to do it much quicker. It's still not a top tier charm, but it's the kind of thing that opens up the option of neat tricks that might not be viable normally, even with sufficient strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23912-scottsman","name":"Scottsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T05:10:30-07:00","id":1219581,"title":"","content":"SFP is actually an Athletics charm in disguise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T08:28:24-07:00","id":1219657,"title":"","content":"Falling Hammer Strike does not enable you to inflict onslaught on opponents with Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1219581#post1219581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SFP is actually an Athletics charm in disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even \u201cin disguise,\u201d it still requires an Athletics roll. I\u2019m honestly not sure what it\u2019s doing trying to be a Brawl Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T08:48:07-07:00","id":1219664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1219657#post1219657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Falling Hammer Strike does not enable you to inflict onslaught on opponents with Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not even \u201cin disguise,\u201d it still requires an Athletics roll. I\u2019m honestly not sure what it\u2019s doing trying to be a Brawl Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would posit it\u2019s a hold over from second edition, as solar brawl was based in part from Solar Hero Style in 2nd ed and it had that charm as part of its conceit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T01:29:08-07:00","id":1219899,"title":"","content":"Could someone please list the purple charms for each type, so I can make a colourblind version?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T02:37:34-07:00","id":1219904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realitycheque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1219899#post1219899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone please list the purple charms for each type, so I can make a colourblind version?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure thing:<br /> PUNCH: Fists of Iron Technique, Ferocious Jab, Thunderclap Rush Attack, Falling Hammer Strike, One With Violence, Knockout Blow, Adamantine Fists of Battle, Fivefold Fury Onslaught, Striving Aftershock Method, Inevitable Victory Meditation, Heaven Fury Smite, Ascendant Battle Visage<br /> <br /> GRAB: Unbreakable Grasp, Devil Strangling Attitude, Crashing Wave Throw, Thunderclap Rush Attack, Oak Curling Clinch, One With Violence, Dragon Coil Technique, Shockwave Technique, Striving Aftershock Method, Superior Violent Knowledge, Inevitable Victory Meditation, Raging Wrath Repeated<br /> <br /> Also note a few mentions that charms should go purple in special cases:<br /> Iron Battle Focus: If you are fighting other Solar (or Abyssal) Brawlers for any reason whatsoever this charm is super good and you\u2019ll thank the heavens for having it.<br /> Wind and Stones Defense : It goes from decent to crazy if used in combination with Reed in the Wind [Dodge] at higher essence.<br /> Dancing With Strife Technique: The reset condition is pretty rare, however, so I recommend this charm more strongly to Dawn castes.<br /> Adamantine Fists of Battle: The repurchase is the second episode, by the way.<br /> Titan Straightening Method: This charm is pretty good on its own, but it becomes truly amazing alongside Raging Wrath Repeated (see below).<br /> Apocalypse Flare Attack: It is worth noting that the text defines the range of this charm as \u201ca foe the Solar can perceive\u201d which can become very extreme with the help of charms such as Unsurpassed Sight Discipline [Awareness].<br /> Heart Eating Fist: But I digress, really, being able to activate Ascendant Battle Visage without commiting motes is a scary thought and something worthwhile to pursue for the supernal brawler that blundered his way into this branch of the charm tree before reaching Essence 3.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T03:51:21-07:00","id":1219914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sagara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1219904#post1219904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wind and Stones Defense : It goes from decent to crazy if used in combination with Reed in the Wind [Dodge] at higher essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fundamentally disagree with this assessment; I think the whole in this case is definitely not greater than the sum of its parts. I mean, yeah, you can pay 3m 2i to increase your Evasion by up to (Essence+5), but... you could already pay 3m to increase your Evasion by up to 5 and honestly, as a high Essence brawler, how often do you run into the situation where you keep attacking the same guy for 8 or so turns and <i>not </i>turn him into fine red mist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T13:02:02-07:00","id":1220072,"title":"","content":"I'm also skeptical about Heaven Thunder Hammer not making the purple category despite the high mote cost. I'd say it can easily be a fight-ender at fairly low levels of Initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T17:15:41-07:00","id":1220136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1220072#post1220072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also skeptical about Heaven Thunder Hammer not making the purple category despite the high mote cost. I'd say it can easily be a fight-ender at fairly low levels of Initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. A short fall averages 5 levels of damage, a medium one 6.8. That basically comes out to 7m to one-shot someone on your first turn. <i>Single Point</i> wishes it could do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T07:54:47-07:00","id":1220251,"title":"","content":"Something that is not noted is that Rampaging Berserker Attack also causes multiple onslaught penalties (as noted by Vance in the ask the Devs) so I think it might be purple territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T14:31:14-07:00","id":1223723,"title":"","content":"Deleted, nm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-31-2018, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T16:14:45-07:00","id":1223752,"title":"","content":"If I understand Superior Violent Knowledge correctly, you are supposed to use this Charm before attempting a decisive attack for which you have 1-5 more points of Initiative than you need. Like, you have 14 points of Initiative, and you're willing to gamble you only need 10 to have good odds of killing your target, so before rolling the attack you store as many points as your 4 dots of Stamina.<br /> <br /> Then, after you've killed the guy and reset to base Initiative, you can break commitment to SVK to recover the 4 stocked-surplus points of Initiative, bringing you up to 7 points before factoring in Striving Aftershock Method's +2.<br /> <br /> Is this not the only time you would want to use this Charm? Otherwise you would seem to be depriving yourself of an earlier turn and the best use of Wind and Stones Defense for no particular reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T17:13:46-07:00","id":1223763,"title":"","content":"I haven\u2019t looked too deeply at this guide, but how do Brawl\u2019s defensive options stack up? Should a Brawler invest in Dodge or Resistance or can Brawl defend them too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T18:17:25-07:00","id":1223788,"title":"","content":"Brawl is notoriously bad at defense by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:21:06-07:00","id":1223806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1223752#post1223752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand Superior Violent Knowledge correctly, you are supposed to use this Charm before attempting a decisive attack for which you have 1-5 more points of Initiative than you need. Like, you have 14 points of Initiative, and you're willing to gamble you only need 10 to have good odds of killing your target, so before rolling the attack you store as many points as your 4 dots of Stamina.<br /> <br /> Then, after you've killed the guy and reset to base Initiative, you can break commitment to SVK to recover the 4 stocked-surplus points of Initiative, bringing you up to 7 points before factoring in Striving Aftershock Method's +2.<br /> <br /> Is this not the only time you would want to use this Charm? Otherwise you would seem to be depriving yourself of an earlier turn and the best use of Wind and Stones Defense for no particular reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uh, that's a valid use but its primary benefit is letting you decisive attack while crashed and thus allowing you to reset to base no matter how far into crash you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:23:16-07:00","id":1223809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1223763#post1223763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven\u2019t looked too deeply at this guide, but how do Brawl\u2019s defensive options stack up? Should a Brawler invest in Dodge or Resistance or can Brawl defend them too?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's strictly a supplementary defense to either dodge or resistance for a serious fighter. You might be able to get away with only brawl if you're not a primary combatant or have a friend with like, Crane Style protecting you, but against decently strong supernatural opposition (DBs and up) it's not enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:44:59-07:00","id":1223814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1223806#post1223806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, that's a valid use but its primary benefit is letting you decisive attack while crashed and thus allowing you to reset to base no matter how far into crash you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's easier to get crashed if you deny yourself Initiative.<br /> <br /> If you kept the Initiative, you have a better chance of acting first in a round and enjoying the protection of Wind and Stones Defense. If you kept the Initiative, you have more to lose before being driven into crash in the first place. If five points would get you OUT of crash, then it would have kept you out of it to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:52:05-07:00","id":1223816,"title":"","content":"&gt; Be at base initiative<br /> &gt; Store 1 of it<br /> &gt; Get withered down to -15 initiative<br /> &gt; Attack someone decisively with your 1 stored initiative plus your MAD DAMAGE BUFFS from being that far into Brawl<br /> &gt; Be at base initiative again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T20:09:49-07:00","id":1223822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1223816#post1223816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt; Be at base initiative<br /> &gt; Store 1 of it<br /> &gt; Get withered down to -15 initiative<br /> &gt; Attack someone decisively with your 1 stored initiative plus your MAD DAMAGE BUFFS from being that far into Brawl<br /> &gt; Be at base initiative again</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit, what.<br /> <br /> How can that be legal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T20:15:36-07:00","id":1223823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1223816#post1223816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt; Be at base initiative<br /> &gt; Store 1 of it<br /> &gt; Get withered down to -15 initiative<br /> &gt; Attack someone decisively with your 1 stored initiative plus your MAD DAMAGE BUFFS from being that far into Brawl<br /> &gt; Be at base initiative again</div> </div> </div> </div>You would still have to contend with the -15 initiative so i doubt you would get to have any damage dice. But that cetainly looks like a nifty way to get out of very negative initiative numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T23:39:02-07:00","id":1223840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1223822#post1223822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit, what.<br /> <br /> How can that be legal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because it says this: This Charm expressly allows the Exalt to launch a decisive attack while crashed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T00:49:07-07:00","id":1223848,"title":"","content":"Whats so great about Inevitable Victory Meditation, and how do you figure it helps against stuff like Hail Shattering Practice?<br /> <br /> It says you &quot;store the result&quot; not 'store successes', so as I read it any 1s and 2s you rolled are still there as part of the result.<br /> <br /> Edit: Reading it now Hail Shattering Practice even says &quot;The Exalt may pay one mote per 1 or 2 in the attacker\u2019s dice result&quot;, which seems to clearly indicate that resulting dice rolls are what's meant by result, not just number of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 06-01-2018, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T01:05:38-07:00","id":1223850,"title":"","content":"Even if you ignore the anti-die trick tech of Inevitable Victory Meditation, it's E4 upgrade allows you to add (essence) automatic successes to your roll. So, for 3m 2i, it's like a deeply discounted excellency on your attack at e3+","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T01:10:44-07:00","id":1223852,"title":"","content":"Also, it does store the successes on the roll. It would be pretty insane if it expected you to mark down how many of each die you rolled in table top play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T01:48:15-07:00","id":1223854,"title":"","content":"2i is generally worth like ~3m I'd say, it's not really that much of a discount before e5 at which point you're breaking the game anyway, and auto-successes rather than dice also nerf your own dicetricks. Though TBH I've never been in a game with someone using solar brawl so I could be off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 06-01-2018, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T01:59:51-07:00","id":1223856,"title":"","content":"Brawl doesn't have any dietricks on the attack roll except for grappling, which is a very situational charm. The 'value' of initiative is pretty contextual, but in Brawl i'd say motes are way more valuable than initiative, which you have no trouble generating. 2i is frequently a negligible cost in my experience playing a solar brawler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T07:17:21-07:00","id":1223904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1223806#post1223806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, that's a valid use but its primary benefit is letting you decisive attack while crashed and thus allowing you to reset to base no matter how far into crash you are.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1223827#post1223827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose I\u2019m at -10 initiative and release Superior Violent Knowledge to make a decisive attack. How much damage do I roll?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1223828#post1223828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zero. As a Storyteller, I probably just wouldn't let you make the attack, so you can't sneak around with damage adders, but that's not the way it works as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, SVK only allows you to make a decisive attack in crash if you stocked enough Initiative to bring yourself out of crash and up to a positive Initiative number.<br /> <br /> Which is a number you would have already been at if you hadn\u2019t stocked the Initiative away in the first place.<br /> <br /> Which would mean the valid use I found is the only meaningful use I can see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-01-2018, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T09:05:29-07:00","id":1223924,"title":"","content":"I get the feeling that the thing Vance wouldn't allow was a intended use - damage adders to create a meaningful decisive while Crashed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T09:55:00-07:00","id":1223940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1223924#post1223924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling that the thing Vance wouldn't allow was a intended use - damage adders to create a meaningful decisive while Crashed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, though the order of operations on the damage calculation is critically important: you don't get to say &quot;Minimum zero damage&quot; and <i>then</i> add Ferocious Jab and Burning Fist Burial, you have to get into positive damage the hard way by adding more Charm dice than the absolute value of your initiative. Which I'm aware is the opposite of what I implied before but I reread the Charm since then and this makes more sense.<br /> <br /> Another trick you can do:<br /> <br /> &gt; Store initiative<br /> &gt; Make a decisive attack<br /> &gt; Reset to base<br /> &gt; Get crashed<br /> &gt; Release stored initiative to make a decisive attack<br /> &gt; Reset to base","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T10:38:32-07:00","id":1223951,"title":"","content":"It`s not that in crash you don't have (or it's negative) a damage pool for decisive attacks. A crashed character <b>can't</b> initiate decisive attacks. Damage adders don`t change that.<br /> <br /> Superior Violent Knowledge doesn't change that. It adds initiative to a decisive attack. If you are crashed, you can't do it in the first place.<br /> Oh, nvm, it lets you do that. Move along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 06-01-2018, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T14:30:18-07:00","id":1223996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1223904#post1223904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, SVK only allows you to make a decisive attack in crash if you stocked enough Initiative to bring yourself out of crash and up to a positive Initiative number.<br /> <br /> Which is a number you would have already been at if you hadn\u2019t stocked the Initiative away in the first place.<br /> <br /> Which would mean the valid use I found is the only meaningful use I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry but that isn't what it says as written. Robert either doesn't like the charm or did not notice the clause that it allows you to make decisive attacks while crashed, which is why he said he would not allow you to make a decisive attack while crashed. That is more like errata rather than a rules clarification, because it directly contradicts the charm as written.<br /> <br /> There is nothing about the charm to suggest that it only allows you to make a decisive attack in crash if you stocked enough initiative to bring yourself out of crash, because there is no rule that negative initiative would be &quot;added&quot; to your damage roll - you're simply not allowed to make decisive attacks while crashed, which this charm explicitly makes an exception to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T14:36:43-07:00","id":1223998,"title":"","content":"The other use for SVK I see is when using Hammer of Iron Technique/Fivefold Fury Onslaught.<br /> <br /> As you divide your initiative between each attack and then round up to make them all the same. So for example if you where to do 6 attacks and you had 10 initiative, there is zero difference in damage between 7 and 12 initiative, so you can use SVK to store 3 initiative to get yourself down to 7. Or perhaps you are purely using these attacks to build up onslaught so you don't care about their damage and just store the max initiative that you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T14:50:06-07:00","id":1224001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1223996#post1223996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...because there is no rule that negative initiative would be &quot;added&quot; to your damage roll - you're simply not allowed to make decisive attacks while crashed, which this charm explicitly makes an exception to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would there need to be a rule to EXPLICITLY state that negative initiative is factored in to attacks?<br /> <br /> A decisive attack uses your current initiative pool for damage unless using an ability that says otherwise. SVK does not state otherwise, however it lets you boost the attacks damage by the initiative stored. You don't just conveniently scrub out the negative initiative in the calculation because you don't like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T15:30:14-07:00","id":1224013,"title":"","content":"Because there is nothing else in the game that interacts with negative initiative. Besides, even if you do factor in negative initiative into the damage equation, you're still allowed to make a decisive attack at any negative initiative value and thus reset yourself to base - as you said, you don't get to ignore the text of the charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T19:16:24-07:00","id":1224258,"title":"","content":"You can't roll negative dice, and the rules for adding dice are that if you go negative and then add stuff with charms, you count from 0. <br /> <br /> So yeah, you do in fact scrub out the negative initiative because you don't like it. That's just how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T19:47:49-07:00","id":1224265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1224258#post1224258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't roll negative dice, and the rules for adding dice are that if you go negative and then add stuff with charms, you count from 0.<br /> <br /> So yeah, you do in fact scrub out the negative initiative because you don't like it. That's just how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can you please provide a source for that? Because even Vance disagrees.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1223828#post1223828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zero. As a Storyteller, I probably just wouldn't let you make the attack, so you can't sneak around with damage adders, but that's not the way it works as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T20:53:21-07:00","id":1224271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1224265#post1224265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you please provide a source for that? Because even Vance disagrees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a disagreement:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1223827#post1223827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Suppose</b> <b>I\u2019m at -10 initiative</b> and release Superior Violent Knowledge to make a decisive attack. How much damage do I roll?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1223828#post1223828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Zero</b>. As a Storyteller, I probably just wouldn't let you make the attack, so you can't sneak around with damage adders, but that's not the way it works as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>If at -10 initiative you would roll zero dice, that seems a pretty clear indication that you can't roll negative dice, no?<br /> <br /> As for not &quot;sneaking around with damage adders&quot;, Vance clearly doesn't like it, but he is explicitly saying that the way he would handle it at his table is <i>not the way the Charm is written</i>.<br /> <br /> So, if at -10 initiative you roll zero dice, and unlike what Vance does at his own table the Charm as written <i>does </i>allow that attack, then one can (per RAW unless Vance issues official errata) add damage adders on top of that zero, it seems to me.<br /> <br /> Personally, I handle it such that, if you have enough Initiative stored to overcome your current negative total, then your decisive uses that positive value, otherwise it uses zero. Have not had the chance to do any sort of extensive testing of that. If it turns out too good for the cost (and I suspect it will), then I'll change it to only be possible to use if you have enough stored Init to get you back to positive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T20:57:38-07:00","id":1224272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1224271#post1224271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see a disagreement:<br /> <br /> If at -10 initiative you would roll zero dice, that seems a pretty clear indication that you can't roll negative dice, no?<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>SVK adds to damage equal to the stored initiative. So yes there is a disagreement.<br /> <br /> If you round negative dice pools to zero before applying charm bonuses. The answer would of been damage equal to whatever initiative was stored in SVK. However the answer was zero.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T02:37:33-07:00","id":1224299,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I\u2019m not finding anywhere that says you get to raise a negative pool to zero <i>before</i> adding Charm bonuses to it, you\u2019re definitely supposed to overcome penalties the hard way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T05:47:53-07:00","id":1224328,"title":"","content":"I was 90% sure the dev thread had said something along those lines at some point, but I can't find it now.<br /> <br /> Doesn't matter though, because Superior Violent Knowledge is clearly supposed to facilitate sudden comebacks like that. Brawl has a lot of stuff that encourages spamming low-initiative decisives and with that comes the risk of Crash.<br /> <br /> SVK is obviously supposed to be a safety net against that. &quot;You can attack while crashed, but only if you're just a <i>little</i> crashed&quot;? Yeah, fuck that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T13:13:09-07:00","id":1224421,"title":"","content":"I'm amused because Incarnated Fury Attack seems broken as hell to me.<br /> <br /> However I'll concede that's because it by-design tap dances on a mechanical fault line of the Initiative System by being a charm about dealing a lot of withering damage to a crashed enemy, which means its power level is ultimately dependent upon how a ST uses trivial opponents and where they would usually call shenanigans on free initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T14:28:38-07:00","id":1224436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1224299#post1224299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I\u2019m not finding anywhere that says you get to raise a negative pool to zero <i>before</i> adding Charm bonuses to it, you\u2019re definitely supposed to overcome penalties the hard way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's nothing that says anything about it either way. The system assumption is that decisive attacks cannot happen during Initiative Crash, there simply are no rules for how it works. At all. I think you can't carry over the assumptions of how damage is calculated during normal decisive attacks. <br /> <br /> SVK is the only charm in the game that creates an exception to this, that means that both interpretations (both Klaek's and mine) of how the charm works are valid. However, personally I think the intent of the charm is to create a sudden low-init comeback as Elfive said, so I wouldn't put initiative in the damage calculation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T14:29:49-07:00","id":1224437,"title":"","content":"SVK is absolutely the kind of charm that needs a sidebar or more in-depth explanation of how it works, because its creating a giant exception to the normal game mechanics. It's uncharted territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T14:44:54-07:00","id":1224442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1224421#post1224421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm amused because Incarnated Fury Attack seems broken as hell to me.<br /> <br /> However I'll concede that's because it by-design tap dances on a mechanical fault line of the Initiative System by being a charm about dealing a lot of withering damage to a crashed enemy, which means its power level is ultimately dependent upon how a ST uses trivial opponents and where they would usually call shenanigans on free initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, you don't generate initiative from trivial opponents at all. Unless you mean the ST not declaring a weak mortal to be a trivial opponent. <br /> <br /> I don't know if Incarnated Fury Attack deserves to be red, but its fairly weak considering the amount of investment needed, its cost, and its usage restrictions (simple + only on crashed enemies). If you compare it to other Brawl simples like Ox-Stunning Blow or Rampage-Berserker, it just looks like a waste of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T14:52:26-07:00","id":1224448,"title":"","content":"I would be more comfortable with SVK allowing you to make a decisive attack, no matter how badly you're Crashed, if it was clear that succeeding on the attack would NOT reset you to base. You still have to survive long enough for your Crash to end, or else use a withering attack like everyone else.<br /> <br /> Incarnated Fury Attack is just weird and bad, and I really would rather use Ox-Stunning Blow or Knockout Blow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T15:00:14-07:00","id":1224450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1224442#post1224442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you don't generate initiative from trivial opponents at all. Unless you mean the ST not declaring a weak mortal to be a trivial opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I mean. Familiars also seem like a potential problem if you can get that much Initiative from kicking the Satrap's dog.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T15:11:45-07:00","id":1224454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1224436#post1224436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing that says anything about it either way. The system assumption is that decisive attacks cannot happen during Initiative Crash, there simply are no rules for how it works. At all. I think you can't carry over the assumptions of how damage is calculated during normal decisive attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, on the other hand, think you can definitely carry over the assumption that, in absence of a game rule saying otherwise, if you have both a penalty (in this case the negative initiative) and a bonus to the same roll the commutative property of addition applies and therefore you don\u2019t get to game the order of modifier application to arbitrarily ignore part of the penalty. It\u2019d be like applying a full Excellency to an Attrbute + Ability of 3 with a -5 circumstance penalty and arguing that you get to roll three dice instead of one. No you don\u2019t because that\u2019s not how math works.<br /> <br /> That said, I do agree with you that Supeior Violent Knowledge should have explicitly clarified whether the above applies, and my preference would be for it not to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1224450#post1224450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly what I mean. Familiars also seem like a potential problem if you can get that much Initiative from kicking the Satrap's dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about, that\u2019s the opposite of a problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Reasons Why The Usurpation Happened #52)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 06-03-2018, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T15:47:12-07:00","id":1224462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1224448#post1224448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be more comfortable with SVK allowing you to make a decisive attack, no matter how badly you're Crashed, if it was clear that succeeding on the attack would NOT reset you to base. You still have to survive long enough for your Crash to end, or else use a withering attack like everyone else.<br /> <br /> Incarnated Fury Attack is just weird and bad, and I really would rather use Ox-Stunning Blow or Knockout Blow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mmm, I don't think SVK is a problem. You seem to be concerned that it is, so let me lay out my argument: For most practical purposes you're ending your crash two turns early - its not something you can bust out as soon as you're crashed because Brawl is pretty restricted on the kinds of extra actions you can do, so you still have a window of vulnerability and any charm you have that ends on crash would still end. Furthermore, there is some counterplay because if you miss your attack you just lose that stored initiative and sink yourself deeper in a hole.<br /> <br /> Is it very powerful? Yeah, anything that expands your versatility in such a big way is going to be very strong, but I don't think its fundamentally broken. It feels about right for a powerful E3 Solar charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T05:43:45-07:00","id":1254977,"title":"","content":"I finally got around to making a colourblind version - apologies for the delay, I thought I'd already done it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_LDdRhmxePfjHTWdO2kOiqpBKw0bqO70REop1Ob9GKE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_LDdRhmxePfjHTWdO2kOiqpBKw0bqO70REop1Ob9GKE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_LDdRhmxePfjHTWdO2kOiqpBKw0bqO70REop1Ob9GKE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_LDdRhmxePfjHTWdO2kOiqpBKw0bqO70REop1Ob9GKE/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T08:09:50-07:00","id":1255004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1220136#post1220136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. A short fall averages 5 levels of damage, a medium one 6.8. That basically comes out to 7m to one-shot someone on your first turn. <i>Single Point</i> wishes it could do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything that negates fall damage negates any benefit of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T07:29:28-07:00","id":1255481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1255004#post1255004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything that negates fall damage negates any benefit of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but we should probably get confirmation that the Air Aspect anima power can basically shut down one of the most iconic Solar Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T22:39:12-07:00","id":1255652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1218958-ed-3rd-brawl-charm-guide?p=1255481#post1255481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly, but we should probably get confirmation that the Air Aspect anima power can basically shut down one of the most iconic Solar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the only one but thats the issue with a gimmick it was the same deal in the older versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T13:37:05-07:00","id":1256532,"title":"","content":"Gonna have to disagree with Cancel the Apocalypse being that bad in practice; anything that lets you shut down something like DBT or Ascendant Battle Visage is powerful enough to get at least a blue imo, we just lack a lot of examples of other Exalted's iconic powers that it can shut down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}